The logic is unchanged. The only edit is a `__builtin_expect` hint marking the "type already set" case as likely, and `profile` is read once into a local. This may tighten the generated code a little, but expect at most a small gain because the function is already trivial.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const auto* p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```